  "worked_solution": "\u0410 second-order linear differential equation has the form\n\n$$\na(x){y}^{\u2033}+b(x){y}^{\u2032}+c(x)y=f(x).\n$$\n\nLet's look at each equation in turn.\n\n- The equation\n\n$$\n2{y}^{\u2033}+(\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x){y}^{\u2032}-y=1\n$$\n\nis a second-order linear ODE with $a(x)=2,b(x)=\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x,c(x)=-1,$ and $f(x)=1.$\n\n- The equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{\u2033}+y{y}^{\u2032}+{e}^{x}y=0\n$$\n\nis **NOT** linear because it contains the nonlinear term $y{y}^{\u2032}.$\n\n- The equation\n\n$$\nx{y}^{\u2033}+{x}^{2}y={e}^{x}\n$$\n\nis a second-order linear ODE with $a(x)=x,b(x)=0,c(x)={x}^{2},$ and $f(x)={e}^{x}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"",
